 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two place particles: 에 and 에서",
     "texto": [
      "**에** marks where something **is**, or where you are going: 학교에 있어요 (I am at school), 학교에 가요 (I am going to school).",
      "**에서** marks where you **do** something: 학교**에서** 공부해요 (I study at school), 은행**에서** 일해요 (I work at a bank).",
      "A useful exception: «to live» can go with 에: 서울**에** 살아요 (I live in Seoul)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Making a negative: 안",
     "texto": [
      "To make a negative, you just put **안** in front of the verb: **안** 가요 (I don't go), **안** 먹어요 (I don't eat).",
      "With verbs made of a noun + 해요, 안 goes in the middle: 공부 **안** 해요 (I don't study), 일 **안** 해요 (I don't work)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs with 해요",
     "texto": [
      "A great many verbs are a noun + 해요 («to do»): 공부 (study) → **공부해요** (to study), 일 (work) → **일해요** (to work), 운동 (exercise) → **운동해요** (to do sport)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
